Floyd rushes into the room and barrels into you. "Oops, sorry," he says. "Floyd not looking at where he was going to."

>
Upper Elevator
You have entered a tiny room with a sliding door to the south which is open. A control panel contains an Up button, a Down button, and a narrow slot.

Floyd bounces into the elevator. "Hey, wait for Floyd!" he yells, smiling broadly.

>
A recorded voice chimes "Elevator enabled."
Floyd rubs his head affectionately against your shoulder.

>
The elevator door slides shut. After a moment, you feel a sensation of vertical movement.
Floyd whistles tunelessly.

>
Time passes...
Floyd absent-mindedly oils one of his joints.

>
The door is closed.

The elevator door slides open.

>
